============================================================
ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA - P2/feature-views/0241 BackupActionsCard
============================================================
[x] Surface renders all states from the web source + the generic standalone states:
    loading (skeletons) / ready (4 backup-section rows) / empty (no backups yet) /
    error (inline + retry) / stale (cached rows + chip) / offline (cached rows + chip);
    PLUS the web mutation states: idle "Run quick backup now", in-flight "Starting..." (disabled),
    success "Quick backup started", permission 401/403 "Quick backup requires admin permission.",
    generic "Backup failed: {msg}". Always-visible action footer (Run + Manage backups & restore -> /backup).
[x] Hooks bound via the shared P1/S8 state-holder seam (IBackupActionsSource over CacheThenNetworkEngine +
    IApiClient); the view performs no HTTP. Operation ids resolve against the generated endpoint table
    (get_api_v1_backup_runs -> /backup/runs, post_api_v1_backup_quick -> /backup/quick).
[x] Every string flows through the ILocalizer i18n facade (BackupActionsCardRegistration keys, English
    fallbacks); no hardcoded literals in native code. Web source is anonymous (0 t() keys) so there are no
    source keys to mismatch.
[x] Accessibility: Narrator names on the surface, both action controls (AutomationId backup-actions-run /
    backup-actions-manage), the status rows and the feedback line; decorative icons hidden (AccessibilityView.Raw);
    success/error feedback is an announced live region (assertive on error); reduced-motion honoured (no bespoke motion).
